Architecture
This is a simple architecture which purpose is to generate telemetry data. 
Four Windows VMs were used to provide multiple independent telemetry sources and allow comparison between affected and healthy instances during troubleshooting scenarios. 
They all have initially Azure Monitor Agent installed automatically due to being connected to a Data Collection Rule. 
The Data Collection Rule sends the telemetry data to the Log Analytics workspace. The telemetry data is then queried in Log Analytics Workspace with KQL.
A broad set of performance counters and Windows Events was collected to provide sufficient telemetry for the troubleshooting scenarios. 
In a production environment, telemetry selection would be reviewed against diagnostic requirements, ingestion volume and cost.

